  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "7 v 5 – get back and defend",
  "description": "Played on a 7v7 pitch split into thirds with cones. Blue attacks with six outfield players and a goalkeeper. Red defends with a goalkeeper and four players: two in their own third and two in the middle third, where they defend at full intensity.\n\nWhen blue gets into their last third, the two red midfielders must race back, get goal-side and help protect the goal. If red wins the ball they counter against blue's goal, and blue tries to win it back straight away.\n\nProgression: play 7v7 with one unit in each third. When a team gets into its last third, the opponents may drop one third – midfield into their own third and forwards into the middle. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Midfielders: as soon as the ball passes you, run back on the inside, between the ball and the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The nearest defender presses the ball carrier away from goal; the others cover the space behind."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The goalkeeper moves with the ball and organises the defence by talking."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "When you win the ball: look forward at once – the opponents have many players high up."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "focus": [
    "defence",
    "positioning",
    "transition"
  ],
  "phase": "main",
